3:["$","div",null,{"lang":"en","children":[["$","$Le",null,{"lang":"en","items":[{"id":"001","slug":"distribution-is-the-moat","category":"doctrine","term":"Account-Generated Distribution","en":{"title":"What Is AGD Marketing? Account-Generated Distribution Explained","dek":"Everyone can produce. Almost nobody knows how to distribute. Welcome to the other side of the iceberg."}},{"id":"002","slug":"ai-sameness","category":"creative","term":"AI Slop","en":{"title":"AI Content for Social Media: How to Avoid Generic Output","dek":"Perfect faces. Interchangeable scripts. Creativity is not measured in exports per minute."}},{"id":"003","slug":"account-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Account Isolation","en":{"title":"Account Isolation in AGD: Build Distinct Social Accounts","dek":"Account Isolation: differentiate the voices before multiplying the profiles."}},{"id":"004","slug":"native-vs-api","category":"lab","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Native Posting vs API Posting on TikTok: What Can You Test?","dek":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need."}},{"id":"005","slug":"agent-first-dry-run","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Tutorial: Preview an AI Workflow with Dry Run","dek":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge."}},{"id":"006","slug":"multi-account-strategy","category":"doctrine","term":"Multi-Account Strategy","en":{"title":"AGD for TikTok 101: Accounts, Content and Your First Tests","dek":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts."}},{"id":"007","slug":"content-isolation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Isolation","en":{"title":"Content Isolation: How to Differentiate a Multi-Account Strategy","dek":"Content Isolation preserves meaningful creative differences between accounts: narrative, angle, format or purpose."}},{"id":"008","slug":"content-saturation","category":"doctrine","term":"Content Saturation","en":{"title":"Social Media Content Saturation: What It Means for AGD","dek":"Content Saturation describes content supply exceeding available attention."}},{"id":"009","slug":"feed-escalation","category":"doctrine","term":"Feed Escalation","en":{"title":"How AGD Changes the Competition for Organic Reach","dek":"Feed Escalation is our editorial term for intensifying formats, output and optimization inside feeds."}},{"id":"010","slug":"attention-war","category":"doctrine","term":"Attention War","en":{"title":"Organic Social Media for Apps: A StudyFetch TikTok Breakdown","dek":"A creator’s StudyFetch video moves from one awkward study problem to the actual app. Here is the structure an AGD team can use in its own product demos."}},{"id":"011","slug":"agd-not-phone-farm","category":"doctrine","term":"Phone Farming","en":{"title":"AGD vs Phone Farms: Strategy, Accounts and Infrastructure","dek":"Phone Farming describes infrastructure for operating accounts across mobile environments."}},{"id":"012","slug":"agd-without-tokportal","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD & infrastructure","en":{"title":"How to Build an AGD Strategy with Your Existing Tools","dek":"AGD is a strategy framework. TokPortal provides infrastructure that can support execution. A category that only works with one brand mostly looks like a campaign."}},{"id":"013","slug":"ten-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD principles","en":{"title":"AGD Marketing Principles: A Practical Editorial Framework","dek":"AGD principles combine differentiated accounts, creative diversity, contextual execution and measurable learning."}},{"id":"014","slug":"anti-principles","category":"doctrine","term":"AGD anti-principles","en":{"title":"AGD Marketing Mistakes: Volume, Copying and False Promises","dek":"AGD anti-principles challenge clones, volume without diversity, certainty without data and averages without context."}},{"id":"015","slug":"native-account","category":"doctrine","term":"Native Account","en":{"title":"What Is a Native TikTok Account? Context and Limitations","dek":"In the AGD lexicon, a Native Account is created and maintained in the real consumer application environment."}},{"id":"016","slug":"account-persona","category":"creative","term":"Account Persona","en":{"title":"How to Build a Social Media Persona: The Duolingo Example","dek":"An Account Persona is the recurring identity that gives an account a perspective: who speaks, to whom, and why people return.."}},{"id":"017","slug":"hook-slop","category":"creative","term":"Hook Slop","en":{"title":"TikTok Hook Examples: Replace Clickbait with a Clear Payoff","dek":"Hook Slop means intense but interchangeable openings disconnected from the content’s actual value."}},{"id":"018","slug":"faceless-account","category":"creative","term":"Faceless Account","en":{"title":"Faceless TikTok Marketing: A Finch App Video Breakdown","dek":"Finch turns a seasonal challenge into a sequence of actions and goal cards. A practical look at faceless content that keeps the product visible."}},{"id":"019","slug":"formatted-account","category":"creative","term":"Formatted Account","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Series: Build a Repeatable Format","dek":"A Formatted Account uses a repeatable creative structure an audience can recognize."}},{"id":"020","slug":"chaotic-account","category":"creative","term":"Chaotic Account","en":{"title":"Duolingo’s TikTok Strategy: Character, Chaos and Continuity","dek":"A Chaotic Account allows several formats rather than one rigid template."}},{"id":"021","slug":"ai-persona","category":"creative","term":"AI Persona","en":{"title":"AI Personas for Social Media: Character Design and Disclosure","dek":"An AI Persona substantially uses AI for appearance, voice or production."}},{"id":"022","slug":"persona-agd","category":"creative","term":"Persona AGD","en":{"title":"Persona-Based AGD: Give Each Account a Distinct Voice","dek":"Persona AGD organizes a network around distinct editorial characters rather than generic brand accounts.."}},{"id":"023","slug":"slideshow-agd","category":"creative","term":"Slideshow AGD","en":{"title":"TikTok Slideshow Strategy: Story Structure for AGD","dek":"Slideshow AGD uses accounts publishing native carousels or slideshows."}},{"id":"024","slug":"story-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Story Slideshow","en":{"title":"How to Structure a TikTok Slideshow as a Story","dek":"A Story Slideshow organizes a sequence around a situation and its resolution."}},{"id":"025","slug":"educational-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Educational Slideshow","en":{"title":"Educational TikTok Content: Turn a Real Process into a Story","dek":"An educational slideshow communicates usable knowledge during reading."}},{"id":"026","slug":"meme-slideshow","category":"creative","term":"Meme Slideshow","en":{"title":"Brand Memes on TikTok: What Ryanair’s Persona Can Teach You","dek":"A Meme Slideshow builds its sequence around a cultural observation or punchline."}},{"id":"027","slug":"product-discovery","category":"creative","term":"Product Discovery","en":{"title":"TikTok Product Discovery: Lessons from the Ocean Spray Video","dek":"Product discovery content introduces a tool inside an understandable use case."}},{"id":"028","slug":"brainrotization","category":"creative","term":"Brainrotization","en":{"title":"Brainrot Marketing: When Internet Culture Helps a Brand","dek":"Brainrotization is our cultural shorthand for fast, absurd and compressed feed formats."}},{"id":"029","slug":"creative-brief","category":"creative","term":"Creative Brief","en":{"title":"How to Write a TikTok Creative Brief with a Concrete Example","dek":"An AGD creative brief connects audience, promise, format and hypothesis."}},{"id":"030","slug":"hook-payoff","category":"creative","term":"Hook & payoff","en":{"title":"TikTok Hooks and Payoffs: A Zach King Video Breakdown","dek":"The payoff is the narrative or practical answer to the opening promise."}},{"id":"031","slug":"creative-library","category":"creative","term":"Creative Library","en":{"title":"How to Build a TikTok Creative Library from Real Examples","dek":"A creative library organizes concepts, versions, rights and results."}},{"id":"032","slug":"format-fatigue","category":"creative","term":"Format fatigue","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Fatigue: When to Refresh a Recurring Format","dek":"Format fatigue is a hypothesis about weakening response after repetition."}},{"id":"033","slug":"creative-matrix","category":"creative","term":"Creative Matrix","en":{"title":"Creative Testing Matrix: Lessons from LEGO’s Instagram Reel","dek":"A creative matrix crosses variation dimensions: audience, problem, angle and format."}},{"id":"034","slug":"niche-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Niche Warming","en":{"title":"TikTok Account Warming: Define a Relevant, Testable Routine","dek":"Niche Warming means exploring niche content in the app through searches, viewing and authentic interactions."}},{"id":"035","slug":"native-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Posting","en":{"title":"Native TikTok Posting: Workflow, Features and Quality Checks","dek":"Native Posting means publishing through a platform’s consumer interface."}},{"id":"036","slug":"native-warming","category":"field-notes","term":"Native Warming","en":{"title":"Native Account Warming: Actions, Records and Limits","dek":"Native Warming happens in the real application through ordinary, authentic interactions."}},{"id":"037","slug":"geo-targeted-account","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Targeted Account","en":{"title":"US TikTok Accounts: Geography, Setup and Audience Limits","dek":"A Geo-Targeted Account is established and operated in its target market."}},{"id":"038","slug":"geo-posting","category":"field-notes","term":"Geo-Posting","en":{"title":"Geo-Posting for TikTok: Location Context vs Audience Targeting","dek":"Geo-Posting means publishing through an account operated in the target market."}},{"id":"039","slug":"us-launch","category":"field-notes","term":"US launch","en":{"title":"How to Reach US TikTok Audiences from Abroad","dek":"An international launch needs an understandable offer and a locally relevant use case."}},{"id":"040","slug":"localization-not-translation","category":"field-notes","term":"Localization","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Localization: Go Beyond Translation","dek":"Localization adapts meaning, references and uses."}},{"id":"041","slug":"account-brief","category":"field-notes","term":"Account Brief","en":{"title":"Social Media Account Brief: Audience, Voice and Publishing Rules","dek":"An account brief sets its promise, audience, voice and boundaries."}},{"id":"042","slug":"operator-handoff","category":"field-notes","term":"Operator handoff","en":{"title":"Social Publishing Handoffs: What to Give Your Operator","dek":"A handoff transfers an executable task with assets, constraints and success conditions."}},{"id":"043","slug":"publishing-window","category":"field-notes","term":"Publishing window","en":{"title":"TikTok Publishing Schedule: Plan Windows, Not Magic Minutes","dek":"A publishing window defines an acceptable interval for a task."}},{"id":"044","slug":"account-inventory","category":"field-notes","term":"Account inventory","en":{"title":"How to Organize a Multi-Account Social Media Inventory","dek":"An AGD inventory connects each account to its role, market, owner and observed state."}},{"id":"045","slug":"zero-views","category":"field-notes","term":"Stuck at 0 views","en":{"title":"Why Does My TikTok Have Zero Views? A Diagnostic Workflow","dek":"Stuck at 0 views describes low or absent distribution after publication."}},{"id":"046","slug":"shadowban","category":"field-notes","term":"Shadowban","en":{"title":"TikTok Shadowban or Low Reach? How to Investigate","dek":"Shadowban is an informal term for suspected distribution suppression without explicit notice."}},{"id":"047","slug":"distribution-failure","category":"field-notes","term":"Distribution failure","en":{"title":"TikTok Publishing Failures: Separate Upload, Access and Reach","dek":"A distribution failure can involve account access, a feature, removed content, a missing publication or weak reach."}},{"id":"048","slug":"native-not-deceptive","category":"field-notes","term":"Commercial transparency","en":{"title":"Organic Brand Accounts: Native Content and Transparent Identity","dek":"Content can be useful, native and commercial at once."}},{"id":"049","slug":"reddit-agd","category":"field-notes","term":"Reddit AGD","en":{"title":"Reddit Marketing and AGD: Contribute Before You Promote","dek":"Reddit AGD adapts account differentiation to legitimate community participation."}},{"id":"050","slug":"community-distribution","category":"field-notes","term":"Community distribution","en":{"title":"Community Marketing: How Brands Join Existing Conversations","dek":"A community is not merely an acquisition channel."}},{"id":"051","slug":"content-rights","category":"field-notes","term":"Content rights","en":{"title":"Social Media Content Rights: A Publishing Checklist","dek":"A provenance register connects images, sounds and videos to their origins and checked usage conditions."}},{"id":"052","slug":"campaign-retrospective","category":"field-notes","term":"Campaign retrospective","en":{"title":"AGD Campaign Review: Creative, Distribution and Evidence","dek":"An AGD retrospective connects objectives, execution, observations and decisions."}},{"id":"053","slug":"budget-of-learning","category":"field-notes","term":"Learning budget","en":{"title":"How to Budget an AGD Experiment: Costs and Learning Goals","dek":"A learning budget includes production, coordination, execution and analysis."}},{"id":"054","slug":"viral-hit","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit","en":{"title":"What Counts as a Viral TikTok? Define the Comparison","dek":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign."}},{"id":"055","slug":"viral-hit-rate","category":"lab","term":"Viral Hit Rate","en":{"title":"TikTok Viral Hit Rate: Define Attempts and Measure Outcomes","dek":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold."}},{"id":"056","slug":"median-vs-mean","category":"lab","term":"Median vs mean","en":{"title":"TikTok Analytics: Average vs Median Views Explained","dek":"The mean adds values and divides by their count."}},{"id":"057","slug":"percentiles","category":"lab","term":"Distribution percentiles","en":{"title":"Social Media Analytics: How to Read Performance Percentiles","dek":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution."}},{"id":"058","slug":"power-law","category":"lab","term":"Distribution concentration","en":{"title":"Why a Few TikTok Posts Can Dominate Your Reach","dek":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts."}},{"id":"059","slug":"top-ten-accounts","category":"lab","term":"Account concentration","en":{"title":"Multi-Account Analytics: Measure Performance Concentration","dek":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome."}},{"id":"060","slug":"matched-cohorts","category":"lab","term":"Matched cohorts","en":{"title":"How to Compare TikTok Campaigns with Matched Cohorts","dek":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics."}},{"id":"061","slug":"posting-time-myth","category":"lab","term":"Posting-time myth","en":{"title":"Best Time to Post on TikTok? Test Timing Without the Myths","dek":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context."}},{"id":"062","slug":"posting-frequency","category":"lab","term":"Posting frequency","en":{"title":"How Often Should You Post on TikTok? Design a Useful Test","dek":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load."}},{"id":"063","slug":"warming-study","category":"lab","term":"Warming protocol","en":{"title":"Does TikTok Account Warming Work? An Experiment Protocol","dek":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing."}},{"id":"064","slug":"account-age","category":"lab","term":"Account age","en":{"title":"Does TikTok Account Age Affect Reach? What to Compare","dek":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior."}},{"id":"065","slug":"slideshow-vs-video","category":"lab","term":"Slideshow vs video","en":{"title":"TikTok Slideshows vs Videos: How to Compare the Formats","dek":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience."}},{"id":"066","slug":"formatted-vs-chaotic","category":"lab","term":"Formatted vs chaotic","en":{"title":"TikTok Content Strategy: Recurring Series vs Spontaneous Posts","dek":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats."}},{"id":"067","slug":"creative-diversity-test","category":"lab","term":"Creative diversity","en":{"title":"TikTok Creative Testing: Compare Ideas, Not Just Edits","dek":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files."}},{"id":"068","slug":"native-features-test","category":"lab","term":"Native features","en":{"title":"TikTok Native Features: Test Their Creative Contribution","dek":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel."}},{"id":"069","slug":"zero-view-rate","category":"lab","term":"Zero-view rate","en":{"title":"How to Measure Your TikTok Zero-View Rate","dek":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope."}},{"id":"070","slug":"confidence-intervals","category":"lab","term":"Uncertainty","en":{"title":"Social Media Experiments: Confidence Intervals Explained","dek":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions."}},{"id":"071","slug":"survivorship-bias","category":"lab","term":"Survivorship bias","en":{"title":"TikTok Case Studies and Survivorship Bias: What Is Missing?","dek":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units."}},{"id":"072","slug":"regression-to-mean","category":"lab","term":"Regression to the mean","en":{"title":"Why TikTok Views Drop After a Viral Post","dek":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes."}},{"id":"073","slug":"cohort-maturity","category":"lab","term":"Cohort maturity","en":{"title":"Campaign Cohort Analysis: Compare Equally Mature Results","dek":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert."}},{"id":"074","slug":"attribution","category":"lab","term":"Attribution","en":{"title":"TikTok Marketing Attribution: UTMs, Visits and First Purchases","dek":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin."}},{"id":"075","slug":"views-to-buyers","category":"lab","term":"Views to buyers","en":{"title":"From TikTok Views to Sales: Measure the Customer Journey","dek":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition."}},{"id":"076","slug":"experiment-preregistration","category":"lab","term":"Preregistration","en":{"title":"Social Media Experiment Template: Write the Plan First","dek":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance."}},{"id":"077","slug":"stop-rules","category":"lab","term":"Stop rules","en":{"title":"When to Stop an AGD Experiment: Budget and Evidence Rules","dek":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment."}},{"id":"078","slug":"evidence-ladder","category":"lab","term":"Evidence ladder","en":{"title":"How to Evaluate AGD Claims: Documentation, Examples and Tests","dek":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore."}},{"id":"079","slug":"ai-agd","category":"machines","term":"AI AGD","en":{"title":"AI for AGD Marketing: From Creative Brief to Publishing Workflow","dek":"AI AGD means using AI to plan, produce, analyze or orchestrate AGD."}},{"id":"080","slug":"agentic-agd","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","en":{"title":"Agentic AGD: What an AI Distribution Agent Should Do","dek":"Agentic AGD coordinates recurring decisions across accounts, content, markets and experiments."}},{"id":"081","slug":"human-api","category":"machines","term":"Human API","en":{"title":"TokPortal’s Human API: Briefs, Native Actions and Receipts","dek":"A Human API exposes a software workflow partly executed by people."}},{"id":"082","slug":"mcp-orchestration","category":"machines","term":"MCP orchestration","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Workflows: Connect AI to Social Operations","dek":"MCP lets an agent client discover and call tools exposed by a server."}},{"id":"083","slug":"dry-run-contract","category":"machines","term":"Dry-run contract","en":{"title":"What Does a TokPortal Dry Run Do? Preview Scope and Limits","dek":"A dry run validates a request without producing live effects under the service’s contract."}},{"id":"084","slug":"idempotency","category":"machines","term":"Idempotency","en":{"title":"API Retry Safety: Avoid Duplicate Social Publishing Operations","dek":"Idempotency prevents repeated execution of one intent from producing multiple effects when supported by the operation’s contract."}},{"id":"085","slug":"webhooks","category":"machines","term":"Webhooks","en":{"title":"Social Publishing Webhooks: Events, Status and Recovery","dek":"A webhook sends an event to your integration."}},{"id":"086","slug":"agent-budget","category":"machines","term":"Agent budgets","en":{"title":"How to Set a Budget for an AI Marketing Agent","dek":"An agent budget defines authorized operations, limits and renewal conditions."}},{"id":"087","slug":"agent-maturity","category":"machines","term":"AGD maturity model","en":{"title":"AI Marketing Automation: When to Increase Agent Autonomy","dek":"The AGD model distinguishes manual work, AI assistance, approved orchestration, agentic management and broader autonomy."}},{"id":"088","slug":"api-slop","category":"machines","term":"API Slop","en":{"title":"Social Media API Automation: Keep the Editorial Brief Intact","dek":"API Slop criticizes mass delivery of undifferentiated content without attention to accounts or context."}},{"id":"089","slug":"content-routing","category":"machines","term":"Content routing","en":{"title":"Content Routing for Multiple Social Accounts","dek":"Routing connects creative work to an account by audience, persona, market and purpose."}},{"id":"090","slug":"creative-clustering","category":"machines","term":"Creative clustering","en":{"title":"How to Organize Social Creative by Idea and Mechanism","dek":"Creative clustering groups content under chosen criteria."}},{"id":"091","slug":"anomaly-detection","category":"machines","term":"Anomaly detection","en":{"title":"Social Media Monitoring: Build Useful Operational Alerts","dek":"Anomaly detection flags deviation from a defined baseline."}},{"id":"092","slug":"human-review","category":"machines","term":"Human review","en":{"title":"Human Review for AI Content: Approve the Version That Ships","dek":"Useful human review exposes the action, consequences and evidence to check."}},{"id":"093","slug":"source-of-truth","category":"machines","term":"Source of truth","en":{"title":"Marketing Automation Records: Build a Reliable Source of Truth","dek":"A technical source of truth describes an interface’s current capabilities."}},{"id":"094","slug":"seo-agd","category":"machines","term":"SEO AGD","en":{"title":"AGD and SEO: Turn Social Ideas into Searchable Articles","dek":"SEO AGD explores social content and properties appearing in search engines and platform search."}},{"id":"095","slug":"pseo-agd","category":"machines","term":"pSEO AGD","en":{"title":"Programmatic SEO for AGD: Structure Useful, Distinct Pages","dek":"pSEO AGD systematically organizes social content around distinct search intents."}},{"id":"096","slug":"llm-quoting","category":"machines","term":"LLM quoting","en":{"title":"Writing AGD Content That Search and AI Can Cite","dek":"Citable content clearly states a proposition, scope and provenance."}},{"id":"097","slug":"knowledge-graph","category":"machines","term":"AGD content graph","en":{"title":"Internal Linking for AGD Content: Connect Concepts Clearly","dek":"An editorial graph connects parent concepts, neighbors and applications."}},{"id":"098","slug":"multilingual-seo","category":"machines","term":"Multilingual publishing","en":{"title":"Multilingual Content Strategy: When to Expand Your AGD Site","dek":"A multilingual publication gives each version a stable URL and connects matching translations."}},{"id":"099","slug":"structured-editorial","category":"machines","term":"Structured editorial","en":{"title":"AGD Article Schema: Structure Text, Stories and Real Examples","dek":"An editorial schema requires publishing essentials: identity, translations, media, stories, text, sources and links."}},{"id":"100","slug":"agent-audit-log","category":"machines","term":"Agent audit log","en":{"title":"AI Agent Audit Logs: Trace Marketing Actions and Decisions","dek":"An agent log connects intent, tool, result and next decision."}}]}],"$Lf","$L10"]}]
11:T585,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","@id":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/read/machines/agent-first-dry-run/#article","headline":"TokPortal MCP Tutorial: Preview an AI Workflow with Dry Run","description":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge.","inLanguage":"en","datePublished":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-09T11:30:08.839243Z","image":["https://theorganiclub.com/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"],"author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Jet","url":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/about/#jet","image":"https://theorganiclub.com/images/authors/jet.jpg"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","url":"https://theorganiclub.com"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/read/machines/agent-first-dry-run/","articleSection":"Machines & humans","wordCount":865,"citation":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/","https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/"]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"THE ORGANIC CLUB","item":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Machines & humans","item":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/topics/machines/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"TokPortal MCP Tutorial: Preview an AI Workflow with Dry Run","item":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/read/machines/agent-first-dry-run/"}]}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main","className":"main-shell","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$11"}}],["$","$L12",null,{"article":{"id":"005","slug":"agent-first-dry-run","category":"machines","term":"Agentic AGD","kind":"guide","image":"agent-first-dry-run","tier":"canonical","evidence":"documented","sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/","https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/"],"related":["human-api","agentic-agd","idempotency"],"tokportal":"sandbox","en":{"title":"TokPortal MCP Tutorial: Preview an AI Workflow with Dry Run","dek":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge.","point":"TokPortal MCP exposes social operations to an agent. A preview uses top-level dry_run: true, with creation parameters inside body; the decision to execute live remains a separate step.","body":["An agent executing everything quickly is not necessarily a good operator. In a paid workflow, its first useful skill is explaining what it will trigger: country, platform, account and immediate or recurring costs.","The remote server is https://app.tokportal.com/api/ext/mcp. The local package documentation requires version 1.15.1 or later for reliable previews: version 1.15.0 advertised an argument it did not forward correctly. That detail matters more than an impressive agent demo.","Read available countries, prices and balance first. To preview a US TikTok account, tokportal_create_bundle accepts dry_run: true and a body containing bundle_type: account_only, platform: tiktok and country: USA. The response should distinguish simulated credits from charged credits.","Preview identifiers are synthetic. Never reuse them in production. After approval, create real resources and continue with their live identifiers. YouTube bundle creation is not supported through this API in the documentation consulted."],"action":["Read countries, prices and balance before previewing.","Check credits_charged: 0 in the simulated response.","Wait for explicit approval before live creation."],"trap":"A dry run validates a contract; it does not reserve real accounts or capacity.","quote":"Autonomy starts with knowing what still needs a green light.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Autonomy starts with knowing what still needs a green light.","text":"A real MCP workflow starts with a readable preview, not a surprise charge.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Agentic AGD","text":"TokPortal MCP exposes social operations to an agent. A preview uses top-level dry_run: true, with creation parameters inside body; the decision to execute live remains a separate step.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A dry run validates a contract; it does not reserve real accounts or capacity.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Read countries, prices and balance before previewing.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Check credits_charged: 0 in the simulated response.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 3","title":"Wait for explicit approval before live creation.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[{"id":"connect","title":"Connect an AI assistant to the actual TokPortal tools","intro":"The remote MCP address is the entry point for an assistant. The screenshot shows TokPortal’s real connection screen, including the authorisation step. Your API key does not belong in an editorial prompt.","endpoint":"https://app.tokportal.com/api/ext/mcp","code":"Inspect my existing TikTok accounts and the current credit rules.\nPrepare three distinct creative angles for a US audience.\nFor each, identify the account, required media and a valid publishing window.\nPreview any proposed creation with dry_run: true.\nReport credits_would_charge, recurring Coverage and missing inputs.\nDo not create or publish a live task.","language":"text","explain":"Copy this as a planning brief after connecting your assistant. It asks for a concrete preview, not a pretend transcript of successful execution. Remote MCP supports the documented dry-run workflow; local tokportal-mcp needs version 1.15.1 or later.","checks":[{"label":"Read-only first","detail":"Choose read-only access when the job is inventory or analysis. Publishing requires an appropriately authorised connection."},{"label":"Discover current tools","detail":"Use the tool catalogue available in the connected workspace instead of assuming a capability from a marketing page."},{"label":"Review before execution","detail":"Check destination, assets, price and review windows against the actual tool response."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-mcp-connect.png","width":930,"height":250,"alt":"TokPortal connection screen with the remote MCP URL and Claude connection steps.","caption":"Actual TokPortal MCP connection screen, captured 8 September 2026.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/developer/connect-ai"}},{"id":"preview","title":"Preview an account with three video slots before committing credits","intro":"The archived builder shows account and video-package choices. This sample MCP request previews a package with one account and three video slots; it does not upload three video files.","endpoint":"POST /api/ext/bundles","code":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_create_bundle\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"dry_run\": true,\n    \"body\": {\n      \"bundle_type\": \"account_and_videos\",\n      \"platform\": \"tiktok\",\n      \"country\": \"USA\",\n      \"videos_quantity\": 3,\n      \"edits_quantity\": 0,\n      \"wants_advanced_warming\": false,\n      \"auto_finalize_videos\": false\n    }\n  }\n}","language":"json","explain":"This is a sample request, not an executed order or a price quote. In REST, the equivalent simulation uses X-TokPortal-Dry-Run: true. Live creation debits credits immediately; the preview is the place to inspect the actual workspace-specific price.","checks":[{"label":"Read the quote","detail":"Read the quoted credit fields and cost_breakdown returned by the current contract. A simulation does not debit the live balance."},{"label":"Keep simulation separate","detail":"Returned simulation IDs are synthetic and cannot be reused in live requests. The simulation does not retain cross-call objects."},{"label":"Review the package","detail":"auto_finalize_videos is explicitly false here. Check the current review-window rules before any live execution."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/sandbox/","https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T11:30:08.839243Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-bundle-builder.png","width":731,"height":655,"alt":"TokPortal bundle builder showing platform and account-plus-video choices.","caption":"Actual TokPortal builder, captured 8 September 2026.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/bundles/create"}}],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Make the preview a contract a person can inspect.","paragraphs":["A dry run earns its name when the reviewer can explain what will happen next without reading the agent’s optimistic narration. For a publishing job, that means the intended account, asset version, caption, time window, cost scope and the action that would cross into real execution. A preview that returns a plausible success message but hides these choices has only moved uncertainty into a nicer interface. Give the reviewer a concrete difference between the current state and the proposed state.","For TokPortal, keep the distinction between a simulated response and a live resource explicit. A synthetic identifier returned by a preview is not something to reuse as if it had been created in production. Before executing a reviewed plan, check current tool documentation and required inputs again, especially when the preview was produced earlier or by another agent. Store the approval against the actual plan revision. If the caption, account or price-sensitive scope changes, the old approval should not silently travel with it. Autonomy becomes useful when the boundary is specific enough to audit.","Treat the preview as a small production meeting with a written agenda. The operator should be able to identify the account or bundle being requested, the country, the quantity, the expected cost and the fact that the operation is still simulated. If the response contains simulated identifiers, keep them out of later live calls. Store the preview beside the proposed inputs, then make any change visible before execution. A dry-run result that nobody reads is only an extra request in the log.","The example payload below is intentionally narrow. It demonstrates the shape of a documented preview request, not a complete autonomous acquisition system. A real workflow must still check current tool capabilities, authorisation, cost and the final live result. If the service returns an uncertain state, reconcile it before retrying. Keep an explicit distinction between prepared, approved, executed and verified. Those states make it possible to give an assistant useful autonomy without treating every fluent completion message as proof that the underlying operation succeeded. The objective is a concrete action a person can understand before it has consequences."],"diagram":{"kind":"flow","title":"A reviewable execution boundary","items":[{"label":"Propose","detail":"Show the exact account, asset and intended action.","value":0},{"label":"Inspect","detail":"Review scope, current capabilities and costs.","value":0},{"label":"Execute","detail":"Use live inputs only after the specific plan is accepted.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"Treat this public post as the final object a publishing workflow would have to reproduce accurately. The video does not expose the system behind it. The useful exercise is to specify the checks your own agent would need before publishing a comparable asset.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T11:30:08.839243Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/agent-first-dry-run.jpg","width":1280,"height":976,"alt":{"en":"A red railway signal glows against a deep blue evening sky."},"credit":"W.carter","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 6efd9fae6123d3472d48491b2d5ae91c124f5c48.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_railway_signal_at_dusk.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en","next":{"id":"006","slug":"multi-account-strategy","term":"Multi-Account Strategy","category":"doctrine","kind":"essay","image":"multi-account-strategy","tier":"canonical","evidence":"editorial","sources":[],"related":["content-isolation","native-account","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"AGD for TikTok 101: Accounts, Content and Your First Tests","dek":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts.","point":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts. It is AGD’s organizational foundation, not its complete definition.","body":["Separate reasons to watch before allocating posts. A cooking app can cover student meals, Sunday preparation and chef techniques. The same recipe does not fulfill all three promises. Extra operating cost should buy learning, not merely more calendar slots.","Consider two accounts covering different uses of a notes tool and a third documenting onboarding. After a cycle, compare the questions each receives. If all attract exactly the same requests, revisit their promises before creating a fourth profile. The next account should address an identified gap. Account count is an input to this decision, not evidence that the architecture works."],"action":["Map three audiences and a suitable format for each.","Assign an owner to every account."],"trap":"Extra accounts without distinct hypotheses make analysis noisier.","quote":"One brand account cannot carry everything.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"One brand account cannot carry everything.","text":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts.","media":"/images/editorial/multi-account-strategy.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Multi-Account Strategy","text":"A Multi-Account Strategy distributes a brand’s experiments across differentiated accounts. It is AGD’s organizational foundation, not its complete definition.","media":"/images/editorial/multi-account-strategy.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Extra accounts without distinct hypotheses make analysis noisier.","media":"/images/editorial/multi-account-strategy.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Map three audiences and a suitable format for each.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/multi-account-strategy.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Assign an owner to every account.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/multi-account-strategy.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[{"id":"inventory","title":"Start with the accounts you actually have","intro":"In TokPortal, a publishing plan begins with a real destination account. This read-only request narrows the inventory to TikTok accounts in the USA. It returns accounts in the connected workspace, not a catalogue of accounts for sale.","endpoint":"GET /api/ext/accounts","code":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_list_accounts\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"platform\": \"tiktok\",\n    \"country\": \"USA\",\n    \"page\": 1,\n    \"per_page\": 3\n  }\n}","language":"json","explain":"Before briefing three narrators, inspect the account IDs and state returned by this request. If an existing account is suitable, choose the existing-account route instead of ordering a new one.","checks":[{"label":"Account ID","detail":"A delivered saved_account_id differs from the stable bundle account listing ID. Use the identifier required by the next tool."},{"label":"Scope","detail":"Results belong to the connected workspace. An empty list is not proof that TikTok has no relevant audience."},{"label":"Next decision","detail":"Match each account to a distinct audience promise before assigning an asset."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-bundle-builder.png","width":731,"height":655,"alt":"TokPortal bundle builder showing platform and account-plus-video choices.","caption":"Actual TokPortal builder, captured 8 September 2026.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/bundles/create"}},{"id":"video","title":"Prepare the actual video slot, not just the caption","intro":"In the archived editor capture, the interface shows Video, Carousel and Story options, plus a target publishing period. The API example below is a separate documented slot-configuration preview; the screenshot alone does not establish the API contract.","endpoint":"PUT /api/ext/bundles/{id}/videos/{position}","code":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_configure_bundle_video\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"id\": \"<real-bundle-uuid>\",\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"body\": {\n      \"video_type\": \"video\",\n      \"video_url\": \"<public_url returned by your video upload>\",\n      \"description\": \"A practical example of organising freelance subscriptions.\",\n      \"target_publish_date\": \"<valid future date: YYYY-MM-DD>\",\n      \"ai_content_disclaimer\": false,\n      \"auto_publish\": false\n    },\n    \"dry_run\": true\n  }\n}","language":"json","explain":"Replace the marked values with an authorized real bundle, a media URL you control and a valid future date. This is a dry-run template, not an executed campaign. The archived UI shows a two-day period for that captured example; use the current API validation response to determine the dates accepted for your own request.","checks":[{"label":"Choose the correct media fields","detail":"A video needs video_url and description. A TikTok carousel instead needs carousel_images and tiktok_sound_url."},{"label":"Use a valid window","detail":"Allow at least three days while account creation is pending, or one day for delivered/existing accounts. Check the current response and limits."},{"label":"Read the preview result","detail":"Check the simulation markers and date validation. If INVALID_DATE includes details.earliest_allowed, use that returned limit to revise the proposed date. Never copy preview IDs into live requests."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/","https://developers.tokportal.com/use-cases/no-code/mp4-delivered-account-preview/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T11:43:29.854908Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-video-editor.png","width":650,"height":565,"alt":"Two real TokPortal editor views showing media format, caption and target publishing period.","caption":"Two cropped views of the real video editor, captured 8 September 2026. Historical dates shown; use a valid future window for a new task.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/dashboard"}}],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Split the audience problem before splitting the workload.","paragraphs":["An easy way to waste a network is to give every account the same product brief and ask for a different tone. Sarcastic, friendly and authoritative are not necessarily different reasons to watch. Start with moments instead. A budgeting app might help someone moving out for the first time, a freelancer waiting for invoices, or a couple planning a shared expense. Each situation changes what a useful demonstration looks like. It also changes the questions that should count as qualified interest.","Keep the first allocation small enough that someone can actually compare the accounts. Assign an owner to each editorial promise, document which formats belong there and agree on the signal that would justify another account. That signal might be a clearly different use case appearing repeatedly in comments or a creative format that cannot coexist with the current account’s promise. It should not simply be spare production capacity. More accounts create review, access, rights and measurement work even when the posting action is cheap. Include that work in the decision to expand.","For a first TikTok test, write three briefs before opening three accounts. Imagine a subscription tracker: one brief teaches a freelancer to spot forgotten recurring expenses; another shows two flatmates settling a shared bill; a third turns a confusing bank statement into a one-minute audit. This is a proposed test, not a campaign we ran. Each brief needs its own visible problem, demonstration and next step. If all three scripts end up saying ‘save money with our app’, the account split has not bought you a meaningful distinction.","Now make the promise repeatable. Emily Mariko’s cooking post below is useful because the process is visible: preparation leads to a finished meal and then to eating it. Study that sequence rather than copying the dish or assuming her audience will transfer to your product. A finance demonstration needs its own equivalent: show the subscription list, expose the forgotten payment, then show the action that removes it. Keep a rights-cleared recording of your own product, with no customer details in view. A satisfying reveal is something you can design; a million views is not something you can put in a brief.","Use one small batch to check whether this system is operable. Record the account, concept ID, original asset, publication URL and observation date in a sheet. Compare posts at a common age, and keep missing metrics blank rather than entering zero. Read comments for the problem people actually recognise: ‘I forgot that charge too’ is more specific than a generic emoji. The TokPortal inventory and video-slot examples below show where destinations and publishing inputs become explicit. They help organise execution; they do not establish that three accounts outperform one. Expand only when a distinct audience promise and the work of maintaining it both make sense."],"diagram":{"kind":"flow","title":"A reason to add another account","items":[{"label":"Distinct need","detail":"A viewer problem the existing account does not serve well.","value":0},{"label":"Distinct format","detail":"A repeatable way to make that problem visible.","value":0},{"label":"Distinct learning","detail":"A question the additional account can answer.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"Read the example as one editorial promise expressed in a post. For your own network, describe the different promise another account would make. The public example does not establish that multiplying accounts would reproduce its outcome.","caseIds":["emily-mariko-salmon"]},"examples":[{"id":"emily-mariko-salmon","platform":"tiktok","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/@emilymariko/video/7010506729012219141","creator":"Emily Mariko","title":"A repeatable lunch becomes a repeatable content idea","description":"Observed refrigerator/freezer access, microwave action, rice over pieces of salmon, avocado being cut, and the finished bowl served with kimchi while Emily eats with chopsticks.","mechanism":"A practical transformation progresses from ingredients to a finished meal. The final eating scene makes the promised result visible.","limitation":"Documents one recipe demonstration. It cannot establish the number of people who cooked it or purchased ingredients because of it.","observationBasis":"Playback started and changing visual sequences inspected on 9 September 2026. Audio and every frame were not independently reviewed.","checkedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","references":["https://media.lsu.co.uk/2021/10/12/tiktok-food-trends/"],"screenshot":{"src":"/images/social/emily-mariko-finish.jpg","alt":"Emily Mariko eating the finished salmon-and-rice bowl with chopsticks, with kimchi on the counter.","source":"https://www.tiktok.com/@emilymariko/video/7010506729012219141","capturedAt":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z"},"breakdown":{"format":"Process → finished result → use","audience":"Someone who wants a practical idea for making lunch.","productRole":"The meal is demonstrated and used. A software adaptation needs its own visible proof.","beats":[{"label":"Give the process a subject","observed":"The cooking sequence works with salmon and rice, alongside kitchen preparation.","reading":"Ingredients give the viewer something concrete to follow. For a software demo, start with the actual input: a document, a messy list or a task the audience already recognises."},{"label":"Show the transformation","observed":"The inspected sequence includes microwave use, avocado preparation and assembly of the bowl.","reading":"The sequence earns its finish through intermediate actions. Removing every step may make a video shorter while also removing the evidence that makes its promise credible."},{"label":"Use what you made","observed":"Emily eats from the completed bowl, with kimchi visible on the table.","reading":"The closing action answers the practical question. A product demo can do the same by using the output to complete a task, rather than ending on the tool’s logo."}],"transfer":{"title":"Finish the job on camera.","scenario":"Original concept for a subscription tracker.","hook":"I checked which subscriptions I was still paying for.","visual":"Use a sample account you own. Show the recurring-charge list, find one forgotten test subscription and demonstrate where a person would manage it. Keep sensitive account details out of the recording.","keep":"A recognisable starting mess and a final action that resolves it.","change":"The audience problem and the proof. A cooking clip is a structural reference, not a finance testimonial.","measure":"Log the destination post and the same observation age for each version. Distinguish completion of the video from clicks or actions in the product."}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T11:43:29.854908Z","author":"spike","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/multi-account-strategy.jpg","width":1280,"height":960,"alt":{"en":"An aerial view of the branching railway tracks at Clapham Junction in London."},"credit":"Mertbiol","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 2f38544bbef93068d0196f4624ed11c612af3a61.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_photograph_of_Clapham_Junction_railway_station.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"previous":{"id":"004","slug":"native-vs-api","category":"lab","term":"Native Posting","kind":"protocol","image":"native-vs-api","tier":"canonical","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":["https://developers.tiktok.com/doc/content-posting-api-get-started/","https://developers.tokportal.com/"],"related":["native-posting","niche-warming","matched-cohorts"],"tokportal":"native","en":{"title":"Native Posting vs API Posting on TikTok: What Can You Test?","dek":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need.","point":"Comparing Native Posting with API publishing requires comparable cohorts and identical observation windows. This note reports no experimental result: the verdict remains unknown.","body":["Two screenshots do not make an experiment. An established account posts natively, a new account uses an API, and someone attributes the gap to the upload method. Age, followers, topic and editing quality disappear from the story.","The protocol starts before publication: define eligible accounts, formats, countries and observation windows. Allocate treatments within comparable blocks and retain technical failures. An analysis restricted to successful publications would answer a different question.","Available native features can differ from an integration’s capabilities. Separate two tests: with identical content and features, does the publishing channel change results? And in actual use, does access to native tools change the performance of the complete workflow?","TokPortal illustrates the separation between API orchestration and human execution inside consumer apps. That describes an architecture; it does not prove algorithmic superiority. A conclusion would need a verifiable method and observations."],"action":["Preregister cohorts, primary metric and observation window.","Keep failures in the relevant denominator.","Report median, dispersion and uncertainty."],"trap":"Attributing a creative or account-age difference to the publishing channel.","quote":"An operational preference is not a law of the algorithm.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"An operational preference is not a law of the algorithm.","text":"“APIs kill reach.” Here is the protocol that claim would need.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Native Posting","text":"Comparing Native Posting with API publishing requires comparable cohorts and identical observation windows. This note reports no experimental result: the verdict remains unknown.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Attributing a creative or account-age difference to the publishing channel.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Preregister cohorts, primary metric and observation window.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Keep failures in the relevant denominator.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 3","title":"Report median, dispersion and uncertainty.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg"}]}]},"workshops":[{"id":"video","title":"Prepare the actual video slot, not just the caption","intro":"In the archived editor capture, the interface shows Video, Carousel and Story options, plus a target publishing period. The API example below is a separate documented slot-configuration preview; the screenshot alone does not establish the API contract.","endpoint":"PUT /api/ext/bundles/{id}/videos/{position}","code":"{\n  \"tool\": \"tokportal_configure_bundle_video\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"id\": \"<real-bundle-uuid>\",\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"body\": {\n      \"video_type\": \"video\",\n      \"video_url\": \"<public_url returned by your video upload>\",\n      \"description\": \"A practical example of organising freelance subscriptions.\",\n      \"target_publish_date\": \"<valid future date: YYYY-MM-DD>\",\n      \"ai_content_disclaimer\": false,\n      \"auto_publish\": false\n    },\n    \"dry_run\": true\n  }\n}","language":"json","explain":"Replace the marked values with an authorized real bundle, a media URL you control and a valid future date. This is a dry-run template, not an executed campaign. The archived UI shows a two-day period for that captured example; use the current API validation response to determine the dates accepted for your own request.","checks":[{"label":"Choose the correct media fields","detail":"A video needs video_url and description. A TikTok carousel instead needs carousel_images and tiktok_sound_url."},{"label":"Use a valid window","detail":"Allow at least three days while account creation is pending, or one day for delivered/existing accounts. Check the current response and limits."},{"label":"Read the preview result","detail":"Check the simulation markers and date validation. If INVALID_DATE includes details.earliest_allowed, use that returned limit to revise the proposed date. Never copy preview IDs into live requests."}],"sources":["https://developers.tokportal.com/mcp/","https://developers.tokportal.com/use-cases/no-code/mp4-delivered-account-preview/"],"checkedAt":"2026-09-09T11:43:29.854908Z","capture":{"src":"/images/tokportal/tokportal-video-editor.png","width":650,"height":565,"alt":"Two real TokPortal editor views showing media format, caption and target publishing period.","caption":"Two cropped views of the real video editor, captured 8 September 2026. Historical dates shown; use a valid future window for a new task.","source":"https://app.tokportal.com/dashboard"}}],"schemaVersion":2,"deepDive":{"heading":"Separate the upload route from the creative package.","paragraphs":["Imagine two posts described as a native-versus-API test. One uses a current sound, an in-app effect and a reply to a comment. The other is a silent export uploaded through a generic workflow. A difference in results would not isolate the upload route. The viewer received different content, and the team may also have chosen different accounts or publishing windows. Before running the comparison, write down every feature available in each workflow and decide which differences belong in the question you are asking.","There are legitimate operational reasons to choose native execution: access to a particular creation surface, an operator’s ability to inspect the final preview, or a workflow the platform exposes only in its own app. Those are capability claims, not evidence of an automatic reach bonus. A useful pilot records the final asset, account context, feature set, publication status and observation window. It also accepts an inconclusive result. If the team cannot hold the creative package reasonably comparable, report the comparison as two production workflows rather than a verdict on an invisible algorithmic preference.","Make a capability table for the actual publishing task before choosing a route. Does this post need a particular in-app effect, an authorised commercial sound, a collaboration setting or an interactive element? Can the supported API perform that operation for this account today? Which steps still require an operator, and how will completion be verified? A plain video upload and a feature-rich native post are different packages. Comparing them without listing those differences lets a technical preference masquerade as an explanation of audience response.","A sensible operation can use more than one route. An API may be appropriate for a supported, repeatable task; an authorised native workflow may be appropriate when a necessary feature is not exposed through that interface. The choice should follow the creative requirements, reliability and cost. Keep a dated record of the capability decision because platform interfaces change. TokPortal's infrastructure is relevant to the execution side of that choice, but its availability does not establish that a native route receives an algorithmic bonus. To investigate distribution, design a comparison that separates the route from the creative features and account histories travelling with it."],"diagram":{"kind":"compare","title":"One comparison, three possible explanations","items":[{"label":"Route","detail":"Where and how the publishing action happened.","value":0},{"label":"Features","detail":"What sounds, replies, effects or formats the viewer received.","value":0},{"label":"Context","detail":"Which account, audience and observation window were involved.","value":0}],"caption":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."},"caseLens":"The original post can help identify the visible creative package. It cannot tell us which upload route produced it. Keep that boundary intact: a recognisable native-looking format is not evidence about undocumented distribution treatment.","caseIds":[]},"examples":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T11:43:29.854908Z","author":"jet","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/native-vs-api.jpg","width":1280,"height":849,"alt":{"en":"Keys, indicator lights, and a rotary dial on a vintage wooden telephone switchboard."},"credit":"Antti Leppänen","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 6750269c8667b0eeec97772aa4c8ec3aa97acff4.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orion_%26_Oriola_switchboard_Elisa_Telephone_Museum.jpg","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}}}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]
